GPIO-TC-001,GPIO Register Defaults and Write/Read Checks,"Verify default register values and masked write/read behavior for GPIO GP0 and group registers.",GPIO clock/reset configured; testbench access to MMIO; known initial pad state.,"1) For each address in addr_array: if readable, read and compare against default_value_array (with mask)\n2) For patterns {0xFFFFFFFF,0xAAAAAAAA,0x55555555,0xF5F5F5F5,0xA5A5A5A5,0xFFFF0000}:\n   - For each address with write_mask!=0 and not skipped, write (pattern & write_mask)\n   - Read back with read_mask and compare expected = (pattern & read_mask & write_mask) | (~write_mask & read_mask & default)",All readable registers match defaults; All writable+readable registers read back expected masked values; No unexpected failures.,https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/blob/main/TestRepo/gpio/gpio_reg_wr_rd_test/program.c,Functional,P1,AutoGen,Draft
GPIO-TC-002,GPIO Falling-Edge Interrupt per Pin (8..39),"Enable negedge interrupt per GPIO and validate RAW/Group status and clear mechanisms via ISR.",GPIO IRQ wired to GIC; sysreg interrupt enabled; pads controllable via 0xA0243FFC.,"1) Configure each GPIO (8..39): doe=1,input; neie=1; iclr=1\n2) For i in 0..31: enable only bit i in GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1; arm wait; drive pad from 1->0 to create falling edge\n3) In ISR: verify DIN=0, RAW per-pin set, group bit set; clear iclr and RAW_STCLR1; verify group cleared; clear sysreg and GIC IRQ","Interrupt observed for each pin; DIN=0 post edge; RAW and group flags set then cleared; no timeouts.",https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/blob/main/TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_negedge_intr_en/program.c,Functional,P0,AutoGen,Draft
GPIO-TC-003,GPIO Rising-Edge Interrupt All Pads,"Enable posedge interrupts across GPIOs 8..39 and verify group interrupt handling and clear sequence.",GPIO IRQ wired to GIC; sysreg interrupt enabled; pads controllable via 0xA0243FFC.,"1) Set posedge (bit17=1) per pin; set DOE input via IO_CTRL_GROUP1..4\n2) Enable GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1 for all\n3) For i in 0..31: drive low, arm wait, drive high to create rising edge; bounded wait for IRQ\n4) In ISR: read group status, mask group, clear per-pin iclr across pins, verify group cleared; clear sysreg IRQ; re-enable group","Interrupt observed; group status set and then cleared; sysreg cleared; bounded waits do not timeout.",https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/blob/main/TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_pedge_all_pads_en/program.c,Functional,P0,AutoGen,Draft